er of a repair storm never converges on that push (it must wait for a whole new push cycle).","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"ff42838866fc93309","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach — Heal algorithm step 1 (lock back-off) vs. Detection paragraph (`healed_once` guard)","norm_id":"n84bc7722f65adbbb","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","scenarios":[],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Have `heal_multi_bundle` distinguish 'locked/no-op' from 'healed' in its return, and in `push_tickets_branch` set `healed_once=True` only on an effective heal; for a 'locked' outcome, apply a bounded backoff-and-re-detect (small attempt cap) so the loser re-enters detection after the winner converges.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"contradicts_reality","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"medium","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Strengthen the credential-less API-surface contract test to assert SIGNATURE/arity, not just names: verify parse_git_url returns a 4-tuple (or unpacks to scheme/profile/bucket/prefix) and that S3Remote accepts the 4 positional args the heal passes (e.g. via inspect.signature or a construction smoke-test), plus release_lock's (ref, key) arity — so helper drift in arity/order fails in the guard, not at runtime.","cohort":["T3"],"criteria":["T3"],"decision":"advisory","drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: contract test 'asserts the exact v0.3.2 surface the heal binds — parse_git_url, S3Remote(uri_scheme, profile, bucket, prefix), acquire_lock/release_lock, get_bundles_for_ref, init_remote_head, and a .s3 client — so a helper upgrade that moves or renames any of them fails loudly here rather than at runtime.'","The heal binds these POSITIONALLY (per Approach step 'constructed from the configured s3:// URL with parse_git_url'): parse_git_url must return a 4-tuple and S3Remote must accept 4 positional args — arity/order, not just name, is load-bearing.","Empiricism-depth axis (a): name-level existence is weaker than signature-level; arity/positional mismatches cause silent runtime failure after ship, the exact failure mode the guard is meant to prevent.","Evidence class: Partially-verified (surface asserted to exist per the plan's live-canary claim) / Unverified offline (git_remote_s3 is the optional [s3] extra, not importable here)."],"finding":"The credential-less API-surface contract test the plan relies on to make helper drift 'fail loudly here rather than at runtime' pins only symbol NAMES (import + hasattr), but the heal binds git_remote_s3 positionally: parse_git_url as a 4-tuple (scheme, profile, bucket, prefix) and S3Remote(uri_scheme, profile, bucket, prefix) with 4 positional args. A v0.3.x upgrade that changed parse_git_url's return arity/order or reordered S3Remote.__init__ positionals would pass the name-level guard and only fail at runtime, defeating the plan's stated loud-failure goal.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fb5c6e12d8518817b","impact":0.55,"is_primary":null,"location":"Testing → 'credential-less API-surface guard' tier; Acceptance Criteria (last box, 'imported lazily behind require_s3_helper()')","norm_id":"na817b14d9eb0921e","priority":0.495,"reason":"default-advisory","scenarios":["git_remote_s3 minor upgrade adds a positional arg to S3Remote.__init__ or changes parse_git_url to return a dict/namedtuple — the name-only guard stays green but heal_multi_bundle raises TypeError/ValueError at runtime on the next multi-bundle heal."],"severity":"major","suggested_fix":"In test_git_remote_s3_api_surface_contract, add inspect.signature checks: assert the parse_git_url result destructures to 4 values and that inspect.signature(S3Remote.__init__) accepts 4 positional params (uri_scheme, profile, bucket, prefix) and release_lock accepts (ref, lock_key). Optionally construct S3Remote with dummy args (construction needs no AWS creds) to catch positional drift.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.9,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"underspecified_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Name the `S3DoctorConflict` exception in Approach step 4 so the described conflict path matches the entity AC9's oracle asserts.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T12","T2","T4","T5a","T5b","T5e","T9"],"criteria":["E1"],"decision":"dropped","drop_reason":null,"evidence":["AC9: 'a content-conflict abort oracle (no bundle deleted, S3DoctorConflict with fsck-recover hint)'","Approach step 4: 'surfaces rebar fsck-recover rather than silently discarding a parent' (no exception name)"],"finding":"The exception type `S3DoctorConflict` is named only in the Testing tier and AC9, but the Approach body describes the conflict path prose-only ('surfaces rebar fsck-recover' / 'aborts, deletes nothing') without naming the exception the doctor raises. The proving oracle asserts `S3DoctorConflict with fsck-recover hint`, so the raised type is a completion-relevant contract that the body should name.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f2c83048341cb9b7f","impact":0.264,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach step 4 vs. AC9 / Testing conflict-path tier","norm_id":"n9e26891a87aaac6b","priority":0.1132,"reason":"low-validity","scenarios":["Implementer reads the approach body and invents a different error surface (return code / log-only) than the S3DoctorConflict the test asserts."],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"In step 4, state that a genuine content conflict raises `S3DoctorConflict` carrying the `rebar fsck-recover` hint (after `git merge --abort` and lock release).","tier":"LLM","validity":0.4286,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"na","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"none","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Capture the deliberate git_remote_s3 private-API coupling decision (why internals, the single-seam mitigation, the v0.3.2 pin) in an ADR / AGENTS.md / adapter-module docstring.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T12","T2","T4","T5a","T5b","T5e","T9"],"criteria":["T5e"],"decision":"dropped","drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'the private-API dependency has one swappable seam'","Absence: no ADR/AGENTS.md/design-doc capture of the deliberate reliance on git_remote_s3 internals is named, only code-level mitigation."],"finding":"The plan introduces a durable cross-component dependency on git_remote_s3's PRIVATE API (S3Remote, .s3 boto3 client, acquire_lock/release_lock, get_bundles_for_ref, init_remote_head, the bundle-key string) — a novel architectural decision. It is mitigated by a single thin adapter seam and an API-surface contract test, but the plan does not state that this private-API coupling decision is captured in a durable design record (ADR / AGENTS.md / module docstring rationale).","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f56a77864484bf74a","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Scope: src/rebar/_store/s3_doctor.py adapter seam","norm_id":"ne49f50bd10da6e19","priority":0.0,"reason":"low-validity","scenarios":["A future maintainer upgrades git_remote_s3 or refactors and cannot find the recorded rationale for why rebar binds private helper internals rather than a public API or its own SDK code."],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.1429,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"na","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"dropped","drop_reason":null,"evidence":[],"finding":"The plan's unrelated-history handling is internally inconsistent and leaves the refuse-vs-union decision predicate unspecified: it claims every fetched head is a tip of the same configured ref (hence always losslessly unionable, so the refuse path 'only fires on a genuinely unrelated head'), yet AC line 9 requires an oracle proving the refuse path DOES fire (aborts, deletes nothing, surfaces fsck-recover). The plan never states how the fold distinguishes a same-ref unrelated head (must union) from a 'genuinely unrelated head while the local store carries events' (must refuse). Sync's analogous gate (_carries_ticket_events at sync.py:80/144) keys off the LOCAL HEAD carrying events — but after the first merge HEAD is the local store and always carries events, so mechanically reusing that gate would refuse the very same-ref heads the plan says to union. Without a defined predicate the implementer cannot both make the fold lossless AND satisfy the refuse oracle.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fd2052bc62e080c93","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach step 4 / Scope (s